# Git Workflow

- Branches: `feat/`, `fix/`, `chore/`, `refactor/` + a short kebab-case slug (`feat/jobstreet-source`).
- Conventional commits (`feat(scoring): cache profile prompt`).
- Atomic commits: one logical change each, with refactors separate from behaviour changes.
- Never commit `.env`, `profile.yaml`, `jobs.db`, `data/`, `.venv/`.
- Never rename a branch that has an open PR, because GitHub closes the PR.
- When changing a rule here or in any `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`, update `CLAUDE.md` in the same commit (and vice versa).
